{"absent":["Locking or concurrency rules for trampoline update, canary publication, and VMCB mutation are not shown.","Numeric values for SVM TSC-ratio bounds and misc2 enlightenment bits are not present in this part.","Exception-stack count and trap-register layout details are not defined here.","Error behavior of guard lookup beyond boolean outcome is not specified."],"dossier":"D10","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/special_insns.h::write_user_shstk_64"],"text":"User shadow-stack store helper reports success when the supervisor write to user memory completes and reports a fault error when the access faults through the exception-table path."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/special_insns.h::nop","arch/x86/include/asm/special_insns.h::serialize","arch/x86/include/asm/special_insns.h::tile_release"],"text":"No-operation, serializing instruction, and tile-release helpers expose single-instruction effects with a compiler memory barrier where ordering matters."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/special_insns.h::enqcmds"],"text":"Supervisor enqueue-command helper submits one 64-byte command from normal memory to a device mapping and distinguishes queue rejection from success through the processor zero flag."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/special_insns.h::enqcmds"],"text":"Enqueue-command submission can transiently fail when the device queue is busy; the caller must treat that retryable outcome differently from success."},{"kind":"abi_constant","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/spinlock.h::SPIN_THRESHOLD"],"text":"x86 spin-wait threshold is thirty-two thousand seven hundred sixty-eight iterations."},{"kind":"export","sids":["arch/x86/include/asm/stackprotector.h::boot_init_stack_canary","arch/x86/include/asm/stackprotector.h::cpu_init_stack_canary.alt_1","arch/x86/include/asm/stackprotector.h::cpu_init_stack_canary.alt_2"],"text":"Boot canary setup picks a fresh random value, records it in the current ta